Experimental Methods in Fluid Mechanics — Pranab K. Mondal (@fd-experiments: 0, is #reference, #part-of @fd-sources) { r_4XFYEGQVB1EV4QF9BP17ME04Y4
Pranab K. Mondal, IIT Guwahati. NPTEL Experimental Methods in Fluid Mechanics, course 112103290. [Course](https://www.nptel.ac.in/courses/112103290) · [Official twelve-week syllabus](https://archive.nptel.ac.in/content/syllabus_pdf/112103290.pdf).

Follow the complete public course during the experimental progression. It covers measurement systems, geometry, pressure and low pressure, flow, temperature, irregular flows, flow angle, micro-PIV, response and statistics. Prepare an experiment from the physical question through calibration, acquisition and inference.

The syllabus expects undergraduate fluid mechanics and thermodynamics; use the particular shared steps needed rather than making entire unrelated subjects prerequisites. NPTEL's public lessons and credited items retain their own terms. Registration or an examination certificate is separate from using the learning material. Completing a video sequence does not demonstrate that a physical investigation was performed.

**Return:** [Fluid dynamics sources — books, courses, methods and physical evidence](../Sources.lingua#r_3Y3TVV9VQAB50M2ZSECK5JTYVG).
